{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/onehundredxcodetips.OneHundredXcodeTips\/documentation\/OneHundredXcodeTips\/DebugGauges","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Debug Gauges","modules":[{"name":"OneHundredXcodeTips"}],"role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"tl;dr","level":2,"anchor":"tldr"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"debug_gauge_memory"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Use-Cases","type":"heading","text":"Use Cases"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep an eye on memory usage, cpu, network and disk access of your app while debugging","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Become aware of a memory leak before opening Instruments","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand over the running debug session to Instruments to investigate further"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Debug-Gauges","text":"Debug Gauges","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"row","numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While you app is running and the debugger is attached, select the debug navigator ("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⌘7"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":") and click on one of the debug gauges.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"debug_gauge_memory"}]}]}]},{"type":"row","numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to investigate a problem you see in the debug gauges, click the ‘Profile in Instruments’ button in the upper right."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Xcode opens Instruments with a context fitting configuration and passes the already recorded data to the Instruments session.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can collect more data for the debug session that raised your suspicion."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"This way the chance of finding the cause of the issue is highly increased."}]}],"size":1},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"profile_debug_session"}]}],"size":1}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Xcodetips","text":"Xcode.tips","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/debug-gaubes\/","isActive":true}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"See important metrics of your app while debugging.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/onehundredxcodetips.OneHundredXcodeTips\/documentation\/OneHundredXcodeTips"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/onehundredxcodetips\/debuggauges"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"debug_gauge_memory":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/onehundredxcodetips.OneHundredXcodeTips\/debug_gauge_memory.png","traits":["1x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/onehundredxcodetips.OneHundredXcodeTips\/debug_gauge_memory~dark.png","traits":["1x","dark"]}],"identifier":"debug_gauge_memory","type":"image","alt":null},"https://xcode.tips/assets/32_debug_gauges.jpg":{"variants":[{"url":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/assets\/32_debug_gauges.jpg","traits":["1x","light"]}],"identifier":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/assets\/32_debug_gauges.jpg","type":"image","alt":"Xcode.tips: Debug Gauges"},"https://xcode.tips/debug-gaubes/":{"identifier":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/debug-gaubes\/","title":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/debug-gaubes\/","titleInlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/assets\/32_debug_gauges.jpg","type":"image"}],"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/xcode.tips\/debug-gaubes\/"},"doc://onehundredxcodetips.OneHundredXcodeTips/documentation/OneHundredXcodeTips":{"abstract":[],"type":"t